references incorporate background knowledge about a person, institution, or event;
a target mentions information available in captions, sidebars, or linked pages but absent from the extracted article;
headlines or standfirsts frame an event using editorial interpretation rather than document-internal evidence;
an article is updated after the associated target is collected, creating temporal inconsistency;
a summary compresses several statements into a relation stronger than any source statement;
automatic extraction leaves navigation text, duplicated paragraphs, or incomplete documents.

